Notes

Some standard Android programs do not work very well with the new binaries in /data/local/tmp/sysroot/usr/bin -- therefore it is recommended that
/system/bin/ and /system_ext/bin are placed in the PATH variable before /data/local/tmp/sysroot/usr/bin

The script init_clang19_env creates some aliase for the executables from clang19. The script also creates aliase for each file in /system_ext/bin that is also part of the clang19_toolchain.
The list of aliase created by the init script is stored in the environment variable NEW_ALIAS.
 

Update 07.06.2025 /bs

The test for the execution permissions like this

 [ -x /bin/sh ] && echo ok

does now work in the bash from this tar archive.



